# A CRLF checkout of a script breaks it where it runs: a shebang line ending in
# `\r` makes the kernel look for an interpreter named `python\r` or `bash\r`
# ("bad interpreter"), from a line that looks correct in every editor. The
# sync tool and its helpers run on a Linux runner and under Git Bash on
# Windows, so both are pinned to LF.
*.py text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
# Normalised in the store; the working-tree line ending is left to autocrlf.
*.md text
*.json text
*.yml text
# The codebase-index launcher has no `.sh` suffix, so the glob above misses it;
# backend pins it by path for the same shebang reason. `**/` covers the payload
# copy and the copy a sync renders at the root.
**/.claude/skills/codebase-index/scripts/cbx text eol=lf
